@* CreateProduct.razor — Phase 3.3 (Admin product creation)

   Staff-facing product creation page at route `/Admin/Products/Create`.
   Reached from the "Create product" button on /Admin/Products. Role-gated
   to Admin / Manager / Employee via [Authorize(Roles=...)].

   PURPOSE:
     Lets staff add a new product to the catalog so they can test the full
     shopping flow (browse → detail → add to cart → cart → submit). Without
     this page, there's no way to seed test data via the UI — only direct DB
     inserts or migrations could create products.

   FORM FIELDS:
     1. Name              (required, 1-200 chars)
     2. Description       (required, 1-2000 chars, multiline)
     3. Price Amount      (required, > 0)
     4. Price Currency    (required, 3-letter ISO 4217 — dropdown with the
                           most common currencies; user can also type a
                           custom 3-letter code)
     5. Initial Stock     (required, >= 0, <= 1,000,000)
     6. Category          (required — top-level category dropdown)
     7. SubCategory       (optional — filtered by selected Category)
     8. SubSubCategory    (optional — filtered by selected SubCategory)
     9. Picture           (optional — single image upload, JPEG/PNG/WebP,
                           max 5 MB. Held in memory until submit; only
                           saved to /uploads/products/ when "Create
                           product" is clicked.)

   IMAGE UPLOAD FLOW:
     The picture is held in memory (as a byte[] buffer + an IBrowserFile
     reference for Name/ContentType) until the user clicks "Create product".
     On submit, the bytes are streamed through IFileStorage.SaveAsync
     (in-process — no HTTP roundtrip, no auth/cookie/antiforgery concerns;
     the page itself is [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]).
     The returned URL is passed to CreateProductCommand.PictureUrl.

     WHY BUFFER BYTES IN OnInputFileChange (not at submit time):
       IBrowserFile is a thin C# wrapper around a JS-side file registry
       (_blazorFilesById). By the time the user clicks "Create product",
       that JS-side registry may have been cleared (Hot Reload during dev,
       a circuit reconnect, or Blazor runtime housekeeping) — at which
       point OpenReadStream throws:
         Microsoft.JSInterop.JSException:
           Cannot read properties of null (reading '_blazorFilesById')
       Buffering the bytes immediately when the file is picked (while the
       JS reference is still fresh) eliminates this. The IBrowserFile
       reference is then only used for .Name / .ContentType / .Size —
       plain C# strings/longs cached at pick time, no JS interop needed.

   VALIDATION:
     - FluentValidation runs server-side via Wolverine's pipeline. The
       validator produces the first wave of error messages.
     - The handler does additional business-rule validation: name
       uniqueness, category hierarchy consistency.
     - Client-side validation is minimal — we rely on RadzenFormField's
       Required + Min/Max for the basic checks. The authoritative check is
       always server-side.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<CreateProduct> (Loc).
     Keys defined in CreateProduct.en-US.resx + CreateProduct.fa-IR.resx. *@

@page "/Admin/Products/Create"
@* Policy: Policies.ProductManagement *@
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "ProductManagement")]

@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.CreateProduct
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetActiveCategories
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Queries.GetAllCustomerGroups
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.DTOs
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@using TakOne.WebUI.Extensions
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<CreateProduct> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject ErrorDisplayService ErrorDisplay
@inject IFileStorage FileStorage
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger<CreateProduct> Logger

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .create-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .create-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            .form-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            .price-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
            }

                .price-row .price-amount {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                }

                .price-row .price-currency {
                    flex: 0 0 180px;
                }

            /* RTL fallback for any RadzenNumeric that might appear on
                               this page in the future. The price-amount and initial-stock
                               fields now use native <input type="number" dir="ltr"> which
                               doesn't need this rule (the dir attribute on a native input
                               is respected by the browser for both caret AND insertion
                               position). But if a future RadzenNumeric is added, this
                               rule at least forces LTR direction on the inner input.
                               NOTE: this CSS alone is NOT enough to fix the RadzenNumeric
                               RTL caret bug — Radzen's JS mishandles caret position even
                               with direction:ltr applied. The real fix is to use a native
                               input with dir="ltr", as the price-amount and initial-stock
                               fields do. This rule is kept as defense-in-depth. */
            .create-grid .rz-numeric .rz-textbox {
                direction: ltr;
                text-align: left;
            }

            .category-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .category-row > * {
                    flex: 1 1 200px;
                    min-width: 180px;
                }

            .form-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 1rem;
            }

            .form-error {
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            /* Picture upload section — dropzone + preview card */
            .upload-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

            .field-label {
                display: block;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
            }

            /* Dropzone — a label element wrapping a visually-hidden InputFile.
                                                   Clicking anywhere on the label triggers the file picker. */
            .picture-dropzone {
                display: block;
                cursor: pointer;
                border: 2px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
                text-align: center;
                transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease;
            }

                .picture-dropzone:hover {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.04));
                }

                .picture-dropzone:focus-within {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.15);
                    outline: none;
                }

            /* Visually-hidden but accessible — sr-only pattern */
            .picture-dropzone-input {
                position: absolute;
                width: 1px;
                height: 1px;
                padding: 0;
                margin: -1px;
                overflow: hidden;
                clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
                white-space: nowrap;
                border: 0;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-body {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                /* Let the label receive the click; otherwise the inner
                                                       elements would steal it from the file input. */
                pointer-events: none;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-text {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-title {
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-color);
                font-size: 0.95rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-hint {
                font-size: 0.8rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

            /* Preview card — shown after a file has been picked */
            .upload-card {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                padding: 1rem;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
            }

            .upload-preview {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                object-fit: cover;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-preview-placeholder {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 2rem;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-info {
                flex: 1 1 auto;
                min-width: 0;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

                .upload-info .file-name {
                    font-weight: 500;
                    overflow: hidden;
                    text-overflow: ellipsis;
                    white-space: nowrap;
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .upload-info .file-size {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.85rem;
                }

            /* Help panel on the right */
            .help-panel {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

                .help-panel ul {
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
                    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .help-panel li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .help-panel {
                    position: static;
                }
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Breadcrumb + back button ──
       Matches the "Continue shopping" button on the Sales page: same
       ButtonStyle.Secondary + Variant.Outlined combo. The user asked
       for visual parity between these two "go back to a list page"
       actions, and using the same style on both makes them feel like
       members of the same family. *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageProducts"]"
                      Icon="arrow_back"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="add_box" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Loading state (categories still loading) ── *@
    @if (_isLoadingCategories)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingCategories"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Category-load failure state ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_categoriesLoadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_categoriesLoadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadCategoriesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── No categories exist yet ── *@
    else if (_categories.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NoCategoriesTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NoCategoriesMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadCategoriesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Main form ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="create-grid">
            @* LEFT — form fields *@
            <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                <EditForm Model="@_model" OnValidSubmit="@HandleSubmitAsync" FormName="createProduct">
                    <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                    @* Server-side error banner (e.g. "Product name already exists") *@
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_submitError))
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                     Text="@_submitError"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Class="form-error" />
                    }

                    <div class="form-section">
                        @* Name *@
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.Name"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldNamePlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                        <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.Name)" />

                        @* Description *@
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldDescription"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextArea @bind-Value="_model.Description"
                                                Placeholder="@Loc["FieldDescriptionPlaceholder"]"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                Rows="4"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.Description)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Price (amount + currency) *@
                        <div>
                            <div class="price-row">
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldPriceAmount"]" Class="price-amount">
                                    @* Plain HTML <input type="number"> instead of RadzenNumeric.
                                       WHY: RadzenNumeric's internal JS mishandles caret
                                       positioning in RTL (fa-IR) mode — even though CSS
                                       direction:ltr makes the cursor LOOK like it's at the
                                       end of the value, typing inserts the character at the
                                       BEGINNING, turning a "1" + typed "0" into "01" instead
                                       of "10". The fix is to bypass Radzen's JS entirely
                                       with a native <input type="number"> and an explicit
                                       dir="ltr" attribute. The browser's native input
                                       handling respects dir="ltr" correctly for both caret
                                       position AND character insertion. We lose the spinner
                                       arrows but gain correct behavior. The .rz-textbox
                                       class keeps the visual style consistent with other
                                       Radzen form fields on the page.
                                       Binding notes:
                                       - @bind uses onchange (fires on blur / Enter) — same
                                         as RadzenNumeric's default, so the UX is unchanged.
                                       - @bind:culture ensures the decimal is parsed using
                                         the current culture's number format (so fa-IR's
                                         "۱۰" and en-US's "10" both parse correctly). *@
                                    <input type="number"
                                           class="rz-textbox"
                                           dir="ltr"
                                           step="0.01"
                                           min="0.01"
                                           @bind="_model.PriceAmount"
                                           @bind:culture="CultureInfo.CurrentCulture"
                                           style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldPriceCurrency"]" Class="price-currency">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="string"
                                                    @bind-Value="_model.PriceCurrency"
                                                    Data="_currencyOptions"
                                                    TextProperty="DisplayName"
                                                    ValueProperty="Code"
                                                    AllowFiltering="true"
                                                    AllowCustomValue="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CurrencyPlaceholder"]"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                            </div>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.PriceAmount)" />
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.PriceCurrency)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Initial stock *@
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldInitialStock"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                @* Same RTL-caret fix as the PriceAmount input above —
                                   see that comment for the full explanation. Native
                                   <input type="number"> with dir="ltr" bypasses the
                                   RadzenNumeric JS that mishandles caret position in
                                   fa-IR mode. *@
                                <input type="number"
                                       class="rz-textbox"
                                       dir="ltr"
                                       step="1"
                                       min="0"
                                       @bind="_model.InitialStockQuantity"
                                       @bind:culture="CultureInfo.CurrentCulture"
                                       style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.InitialStockQuantity)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Category hierarchy — three dropdowns in a row. *@
                        <div>
                            <div class="category-row">
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_model.CategoryId"
                                                    Data="_categories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CategoryPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnCategoryChanged"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_model.SubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["OptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnSubCategoryChanged"
                                                    Disabled="@(_model.CategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubSubCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    @bind-Value="_model.SubSubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["OptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    Disabled="@(_model.SubCategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                            </div>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.CategoryId)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Picture upload (optional) — dropzone-style UI *@
                        <div class="upload-section">
                            <label class="field-label">@Loc["FieldPicture"]</label>

                            @if (_selectedFile is null)
                            {
                                @* Dropzone — clickable label wrapping a visually-hidden InputFile. *@
                                <label class="picture-dropzone">
                                    <InputFile OnChange="@OnInputFileChange"
                                               accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp"
                                               class="picture-dropzone-input" />
                                    <div class="picture-dropzone-body">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="cloud_upload"
                                                    Style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                                        <div class="picture-dropzone-text">
                                            <span class="picture-dropzone-title">@Loc["UploadDropzoneTitle"]</span>
                                            <span class="picture-dropzone-hint">@Loc["UploadDropzoneHint"]</span>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </label>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                @* Preview card — larger preview + Danger-styled Remove button *@
                                <div class="upload-card">
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_previewDataUrl))
                                    {
                                        <img src="@_previewDataUrl" alt="preview" class="upload-preview" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <div class="upload-preview-placeholder">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="image" />
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                    <div class="upload-info">
                                        <div class="file-name">@_selectedFile.Name</div>
                                        <div class="file-size">@FormatBytes(_selectedFile.Size)</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveImage"]"
                                                  Icon="delete"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Click="@RemoveImage" />
                                </div>

                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block;">
                                    @Loc["PictureHint"]
                                </RadzenText>
                            }

                            @* Upload validation error (shown in either state) *@
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_uploadError))
                            {
                                <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["UploadErrorTitle"]"
                                             Text="@_uploadError"
                                             AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                             Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                             ShowIcon="true" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* ── Per-group purchase limits editor ──
                           Shows ALL existing customer groups with a limit input
                           for each, pre-filled with the domain default (1).
                           The user can override any value — the handler's
                           auto-default loop will replace the default with the
                           user-specified override (or leave it at 1 if the
                           user keeps the default).
                           SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): the "Add custom group name"
                           flow is gone — admins must create groups via the
                           CreateGroup page first. Every limit row references
                           a real CustomerGroup row.
                           The Product aggregate owns the domain value-object
                           creation (CustomerGroupPurchaseLimit) — the command
                           only carries a flat DTO and the handler delegates
                           to Product.SetPurchaseLimit. *@
                        <div class="form-section">
                            <label class="field-label" style="margin: 0;">@Loc["FieldPurchaseLimits"]</label>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block;">
                                @Loc["PurchaseLimitsHint"]
                            </RadzenText>

                            @if (_isLoadingGroups)
                            {
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); padding: 0.5rem 0;">
                                    @Loc["LoadingGroups"]
                                </RadzenText>
                            }
                            else if (_model.PurchaseLimits.Count == 0)
                            {
                                <div style="padding: 0.5rem 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                        @Loc["NoLimitRows"]
                                    </RadzenText>
                                    @* SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): when no groups exist, the admin
                                       can't set per-group limits here. They can still create the
                                       product (the handler's auto-default loop is a no-op when
                                       there are no groups). Provide a link to create a group first. *@
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionCreateGroup"]"
                                                  Icon="group_add"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
                                </div>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                                    @for (var i = 0; i < _model.PurchaseLimits.Count; i++)
                                    {
                                        var row = _model.PurchaseLimits[i];
                                        <div style="display: flex; align-items: end; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitGroup"]"
                                                             Style="flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 160px;">
                                                @* Existing group — read-only display (no editing the name,
                                                   just the limit). SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): all rows are
                                                   existing-group rows now (the "Add custom group name"
                                                   flow was removed — admins must create groups via the
                                                   CreateGroup page first). The group NAME is display-only;
                                                   the GroupId is what gets passed to the command. *@
                                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1"
                                                            Style="display: block; padding: 0.5rem 0; font-weight: 600;">
                                                    @row.GroupName
                                                </RadzenText>
                                            </RadzenFormField>
                                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitValue"]"
                                                             Style="flex: 0 1 120px; min-width: 100px;">
                                                <RadzenNumeric @bind-Value="row.Limit"
                                                               TValue="int?"
                                                               Min="1"
                                                               Max="10000"
                                                               Placeholder="@Loc["LimitValuePlaceholder"]"
                                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                                            </RadzenFormField>
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* Form actions *@
                        <div class="form-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                          Icon="close"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)"
                                          Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SubmitButton"]"
                                          Icon="save"
                                          ButtonType="ButtonType.Submit"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </EditForm>
            </RadzenCard>

            @* RIGHT — help panel (sticky on desktop) *@
            <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="help-panel" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["HelpTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                </RadzenStack>
                <ul>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpNameUnique"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPrice"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpStock"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpCategory"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPicture"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPurchaseLimits"]</li>
                </ul>
            </RadzenCard>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Form model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private sealed class CreateProductFormModel
    {
        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
        public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
        public decimal PriceAmount { get; set; } = 1m;
        // Default currency is IRR (Iranian Rial) — the user's primary
        // market is Iran, so the default should match. Staff creating
        // products in USD/EUR/etc. can switch the dropdown.
        public string PriceCurrency { get; set; } = "IRR";
        public int InitialStockQuantity { get; set; } = 0;
        public Guid? CategoryId { get; set; }
        public Guid? SubCategoryId { get; set; }
        public Guid? SubSubCategoryId { get; set; }

        // PictureUrl is NOT on the form model. The picture is held in
        // memory as IBrowserFile? _selectedFile (captured by the
        // InputFile component) and only converted to a URL when the
        // user submits — the file is streamed through IFileStorage
        // and the returned URL is passed directly to CreateProductCommand.

        /// <summary>
        /// Per-group purchase limits being edited. Each entry maps to a
        /// PurchaseLimitInputDto in the command. Empty list = no limits.
        /// </summary>
        public List<PurchaseLimitRow> PurchaseLimits { get; set; } = new();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One row in the per-group purchase-limit editor. Bound to the UI
    /// (read-only group-name label + RadzenNumeric for the limit).
    /// Converted to <c>PurchaseLimitInputDto</c> at submit time.
    ///
    /// SALARY FEATURE (Step 8):
    ///   The row now carries <c>GroupId</c> (Guid FK to CustomerGroups.Id)
    ///   instead of a free-text group name. The <c>GroupName</c> field is
    ///   DISPLAY-ONLY (read from the source CustomerGroupListItemDto). The
    ///   "Add custom group name" flow is gone — admins must create groups
    ///   via the CreateGroup page first, so every limit row references a
    ///   real CustomerGroup row.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class PurchaseLimitRow
    {
        /// <summary>
        /// The customer group Id this limit applies to. Set once at row
        /// creation (from CustomerGroupListItemDto.Id). Never mutated by
        /// the UI — the group name is read-only, only the Limit is editable.
        /// </summary>
        public Guid GroupId { get; init; }

        /// <summary>
        /// The customer group's DISPLAY NAME (read from
        /// CustomerGroupListItemDto.Name). Used only for rendering —
        /// never passed to the command (the command takes GroupId).
        /// </summary>
        public string GroupName { get; init; } = string.Empty;

        /// <summary>
        /// The limit value. Pre-filled with <c>CustomerGroupPurchaseLimit.DefaultLimit</c>
        /// (1) so the user sees the system default — they can override
        /// with any value &gt;= 1. The handler's auto-default loop will
        /// overwrite with this value (effectively a no-op if the user
        /// keeps 1; a real override if the user changes it).
        /// </summary>
        public int? Limit { get; set; }
    }

    private CreateProductFormModel _model = new();

    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<CategoryDto> _categories = new();
    private List<SubCategoryDto> _availableSubCategories = new();
    private List<SubSubCategoryDto> _availableSubSubCategories = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Distinct customer groups that currently exist in the system.
    /// Loaded once on page init via GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery. Each group
    /// seeds a row in the purchase-limits editor (every existing group is
    /// shown with its default limit pre-filled — the user can override).
    /// SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): the type changed from List&lt;string&gt; to
    /// List&lt;CustomerGroupListItemDto&gt; so each row carries both Id and Name.
    /// </summary>
    private List<CustomerGroupListItemDto> _existingGroups = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// True while GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery is in flight. The purchase-limits
    /// editor shows a "loading" placeholder until the existing-group rows
    /// are seeded (so the user doesn't see an empty list flash before the
    /// real rows appear).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isLoadingGroups = true;

    private bool _isLoadingCategories = true;
    private string? _categoriesLoadError;
    private bool _isSubmitting;
    private string? _submitError;

    // ── Deferred image-upload state ─────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The file is captured in memory as an IBrowserFile (via Blazor's
    // InputFile component) and only saved via IFileStorage during the
    // submit handler. The file is held server-side in the Blazor circuit's
    // memory; nothing is written to disk until "Create product" is
    // clicked. If the user cancels or validation fails, no file is
    // saved.
    //
    // - _selectedFile:        the IBrowserFile picked by the user. Used
    //                          for .Name / .ContentType / .Size only —
    //                          NOT for reading bytes (see _selectedFileBytes).
    // - _selectedFileBytes:   the file's bytes, buffered IMMEDIATELY in
    //                          OnInputFileChange while the JS-side
    //                          _blazorFilesById registry is still valid.
    //                          This is the fix for the
    //                          "Cannot read properties of null (reading '_blazorFilesById')"
    //                          JSException that occurred when reading
    //                          bytes at submit time after the registry
    //                          had been cleared by Hot Reload / circuit
    //                          reconnect / runtime housekeeping.
    // - _previewDataUrl:      a downscaled data: URL for the preview
    //                          thumbnail (400×400 max).
    // - _alreadyUploadedUrl:  the URL returned by IFileStorage on a
    //                          previous successful upload attempt during
    //                          THIS form's lifetime. If the command then
    //                          fails (e.g. name not unique) and the user
    //                          retries, we reuse this URL instead of
    //                          re-uploading — avoiding duplicate orphan
    //                          files under /uploads/products/.
    // - _uploadError:         validation error message from the upload
    //                          step (wrong type, too large, etc.).
    // - _isUploading:         true during the IFileStorage.SaveAsync call.

    private IBrowserFile? _selectedFile;
    private byte[]? _selectedFileBytes;
    private string? _previewDataUrl;
    private string? _alreadyUploadedUrl;
    private string? _uploadError;
    private bool _isUploading;

    /// <summary>
    /// Maximum accepted file size (matches LocalFileStorage's cap).
    /// Enforced client-side via IBrowserFile.Size check + OpenReadStream
    /// (which throws if the stream exceeds the limit).
    /// </summary>
    private const long MaxFileSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5 MB

    /// <summary>
    /// Content types accepted by the upload. Matches the allowlist in
    /// LocalFileStorage. Validated client-side here for immediate
    /// feedback; validated again server-side as defense-in-depth.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly HashSet<string> AllowedContentTypes = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    {
        "image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/webp"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The most common ISO 4217 currency codes. The user can also
    /// type a custom 3-letter code via the dropdown's
    /// AllowCustomValue=true (e.g. "BTC", "CHF").
    ///
    /// DISPLAY FORMAT (per the user's spec):
    ///   - In fa-IR (Persian) UI:  "IRR (ریال)"
    ///   - In en-US (English) UI:  "IRR (Rial)"
    /// Only the matching language's name is shown — the code is
    /// always Latin (ISO 4217) so it's recognizable in both UIs.
    /// </summary>
    private readonly List<CurrencyOption> _currencyOptions = new()
    {
        new() { Code = "IRR", EnglishName = "Rial",           PersianName = "ریال" },
        new() { Code = "USD", EnglishName = "US dollar",      PersianName = "دلار" },
        new() { Code = "EUR", EnglishName = "Euro",           PersianName = "یورو" },
        new() { Code = "GBP", EnglishName = "Pound sterling", PersianName = "پوند" },
        new() { Code = "JPY", EnglishName = "Japanese yen",   PersianName = "ین ژاپن" },
        new() { Code = "CNY", EnglishName = "Chinese yuan",   PersianName = "یوآن چین" },
        new() { Code = "AED", EnglishName = "UAE dirham",     PersianName = "درهم امارات" },
        new() { Code = "TRY", EnglishName = "Turkish lira",   PersianName = "لیر ترکیه" },
        new() { Code = "CAD", EnglishName = "Canadian dollar", PersianName = "دلار کانادا" },
        new() { Code = "AUD", EnglishName = "Australian dollar", PersianName = "دلار استرالیا" }
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// One row in the currency dropdown. The RadzenDropDown binds to
    /// Code (ValueProperty) and displays DisplayName (TextProperty).
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class CurrencyOption
    {
        public string Code { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string EnglishName { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string PersianName { get; init; } = string.Empty;

        /// <summary>
        /// Culture-aware display string. Reads CurrentUICulture on
        /// every access (called during render) so it picks up
        /// language switches without us needing to rebuild the list:
        ///   - fa-IR → "IRR (ریال)"
        ///   - en-US → "IRR (Rial)"
        /// The ISO code is always Latin so it's recognizable in
        /// either UI; only the parenthesized name switches language.
        /// </summary>
        public string DisplayName =>
            System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.Name
                .StartsWith("fa", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                ? $"{Code} ({PersianName})"
                : $"{Code} ({EnglishName})";
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Load categories + existing group names in parallel — both are
        // independent reads needed to render the form.
        await Task.WhenAll(LoadCategoriesAsync(), LoadGroupNamesAsync());
    }

    // ── Image selection handlers ────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task OnInputFileChange(InputFileChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        _uploadError = null;

        // User cancelled the OS file picker — keep the previous selection.
        if (e.FileCount == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        var file = e.File;

        // ── Validate content type.
        if (!AllowedContentTypes.Contains(file.ContentType))
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidType"];
            _selectedFile = null;
            _selectedFileBytes = null;
            _previewDataUrl = null;
            _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
            return;
        }

        // ── Validate size.
        if (file.Size > MaxFileSize)
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidSize"];
            _selectedFile = null;
            _selectedFileBytes = null;
            _previewDataUrl = null;
            _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
            return;
        }

        // ── Accept the file. Clear any previous upload URL — picking a
        //    new file invalidates a previous successful upload.
        _selectedFile = file;
        _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;

        // ── Buffer the file bytes NOW while the IBrowserFile reference is
        //    still valid. The JS-side _blazorFilesById registry that backs
        //    IBrowserFile can become null by the time the user clicks
        //    "Create product" (Hot Reload, circuit reconnect, or just time
        //    passing in dev) — at which point OpenReadStream throws:
        //      JSException: Cannot read properties of null (reading '_blazorFilesById')
        //    Buffering here is safe because we've already validated
        //    file.Size <= 5 MB.
        try
        {
            await using var readStream = file.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: MaxFileSize);
            using var ms = new MemoryStream();
            await readStream.CopyToAsync(ms);
            _selectedFileBytes = ms.ToArray();
        }
        catch
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadErrorGeneric"];
            _selectedFile = null;
            _selectedFileBytes = null;
            _previewDataUrl = null;
            _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
            return;
        }

        _previewDataUrl = await GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(file);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Generates a downscaled data: URL preview of the selected image.
    /// Uses IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync which produces a server-
    /// side resized copy (max 400×400). Best-effort: returns null if
    /// preview generation fails.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<string?> GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(IBrowserFile file)
    {
        try
        {
            var resized = await file.RequestImageFileAsync(file.ContentType, 400, 400);
            await using var stream = resized.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: 2 * 1024 * 1024);
            using var ms = new MemoryStream();
            await stream.CopyToAsync(ms);
            var base64 = Convert.ToBase64String(ms.ToArray());
            return $"data:{file.ContentType};base64,{base64}";
        }
        catch
        {
            return null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Clears the selected file + preview + any cached upload URL.
    /// </summary>
    private void RemoveImage()
    {
        _selectedFile = null;
        _selectedFileBytes = null;
        _previewDataUrl = null;
        _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
        _uploadError = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a byte count as a human-readable string (e.g. "1.2 MB").
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatBytes(long bytes)
    {
        string[] units = { "B", "KB", "MB", "GB" };
        double size = bytes;
        int unit = 0;
        while (size >= 1024 && unit < units.Length - 1)
        {
            size /= 1024;
            unit++;
        }
        return $"{size:0.#} {units[unit]}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Saves the selected file to durable storage via IFileStorage.
    /// Returns the public URL on success, or an error message on failure.
    ///
    /// Uses the buffered _selectedFileBytes (NOT _selectedFile.OpenReadStream)
    /// to avoid the JSException that occurs when the JS-side
    /// _blazorFilesById registry has been cleared by the time submit runs.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<(string? Url, string? Error)> UploadSelectedFileAsync()
    {
        if (_selectedFile is null || _selectedFileBytes is null)
        {
            return (Url: null, Error: null);
        }

        try
        {
            // Use the buffered bytes, not the (potentially stale) IBrowserFile.
            // MemoryStream over a byte[] is non-seekable for write but seekable
            // for read — which is all LocalFileStorage needs.
            using var stream = new MemoryStream(_selectedFileBytes, writable: false);

            var url = await FileStorage.SaveAsync(
                stream,
                _selectedFile.Name,
                _selectedFile.ContentType,
                CancellationToken.None);

            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
            {
                return (Url: null, Error: Loc["UploadErrorResponseFormat"]);
            }

            return (Url: url, Error: null);
        }
        catch (System.IO.InvalidDataException ex)
        {
            // LocalFileStorage throws InvalidDataException for: unrecognized
            // content type, content-type mismatch, or file size over limit.
            return (Url: null, Error: ex.Message);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Log the full exception server-side via the structured ILogger
            // pipeline (v4 #15: replaced Console.Error.WriteLine that dumped
            // ex.GetType().FullName + ex.StackTrace to stdout — ILogger
            // captures the full type name + stack trace server-side
            // without leaking them to the container's stdout log driver).
            //
            // Surface a wire-format unexpected error so the consumer
            // (HandleSubmitAsync) recognizes the UE| prefix and routes
            // through ErrorDisplay.Localize for the localized message +
            // visible code.
            Logger.LogError(ex, "UploadSelectedFileAsync failed");
            return (Url: null, Error: $"{ErrorDisplayService.WireFormatPrefix}{UnexpectedErrorCodes.CreateProduct_UploadFailure}");
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadCategoriesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingCategories = true;
        _categoriesLoadError = null;

        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CategoryDto>>>(
                new GetActiveCategoriesQuery());

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _categories = result.Value;
            }
            else
            {
                _categoriesLoadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _categoriesLoadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingCategories = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads all active customer groups and seeds one row per group in the
    /// purchase-limits editor. Each row is pre-filled with the domain
    /// <c>CustomerGroupPurchaseLimit.DefaultLimit</c> (1) — the user can
    /// override any value to set a custom limit, or leave it as the default.
    /// The CreateProductCommandHandler runs its own auto-default loop too,
    /// so the submitted values act as overrides on top of the default.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadGroupNamesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingGroups = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CustomerGroupListItemDto>>>(
                new GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery { IncludeInactive = false });

            if (result.IsSuccess && result.Value is not null)
            {
                _existingGroups = result.Value
                    .OrderBy(g => g.Name, StringComparer.CurrentCulture)
                    .ToList();

                // Seed one row per existing group. Pre-fill the limit with
                // the domain default (1) so the user sees the system's
                // intended default at a glance — they can override any row.
                // The CreateProductCommandHandler also runs an auto-default
                // loop, so submitting with all defaults is equivalent to
                // submitting with no overrides (the auto-default wins).
                const int defaultLimit = 1; // CustomerGroupPurchaseLimit.DefaultLimit
                foreach (var group in _existingGroups)
                {
                    _model.PurchaseLimits.Add(new PurchaseLimitRow
                    {
                        GroupId = group.Id,
                        GroupName = group.Name,
                        Limit = defaultLimit
                    });
                }
            }
            // Silent failure — if the query fails, the user gets an empty
            // limits editor with a "no groups" message + a link to /CreateGroup.
        }
        catch
        {
            // Same — silent. The form still works; the product is created
            // without any per-group limits (the handler's auto-default loop
            // runs against an empty group list and is a no-op).
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingGroups = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Cascade handlers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private Task OnCategoryChanged(Guid? categoryId)
    {
        _model.CategoryId = categoryId;
        _model.SubCategoryId = null;
        _model.SubSubCategoryId = null;

        _availableSubCategories = categoryId is null
            ? new()
            : _categories.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Id == categoryId.Value)?.SubCategories ?? new();

        _availableSubSubCategories = new();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task OnSubCategoryChanged(Guid? subCategoryId)
    {
        _model.SubCategoryId = subCategoryId;
        _model.SubSubCategoryId = null;

        _availableSubSubCategories = subCategoryId is null
            ? new()
            : _availableSubCategories.FirstOrDefault(sc => sc.Id == subCategoryId.Value)?.SubSubCategories ?? new();

        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    // ── Submit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Submit is a TWO-PHASE operation when a file is selected:
    //   Phase 1 (upload): stream the selected file through IFileStorage,
    //                      get back the public URL it's been saved at.
    //   Phase 2 (create): Dispatch CreateProductCommand with the uploaded
    //                      URL (or null if no file was selected).
    //
    // If Phase 1 fails, we abort before Phase 2 — no product is created.
    // If Phase 1 succeeds but Phase 2 fails, we cache the uploaded URL
    // in _alreadyUploadedUrl so a retry skips Phase 1.

    private async Task HandleSubmitAsync()
    {
        _submitError = null;

        if (_model.CategoryId is null || _model.CategoryId == Guid.Empty)
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_CategoryRequired"];
            return;
        }

        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            // ── Phase 1: upload the selected file (if any) ──
            string? pictureUrl = _alreadyUploadedUrl;
            if (pictureUrl is null && _selectedFile is not null)
            {
                _isUploading = true;
                try
                {
                    var (url, error) = await UploadSelectedFileAsync();
                    if (error is not null)
                    {
                        _submitError = ErrorDisplay.Localize(error);
                        return;
                    }
                    pictureUrl = url;
                    _alreadyUploadedUrl = url;
                }
                finally
                {
                    _isUploading = false;
                }
            }

            // ── Phase 2: dispatch the create command ──
            // Build the purchase-limit DTOs from the form rows. Every row
            // carries a non-empty GroupId (set at row creation) and a Limit
            // pre-filled with the default (1). The user can change the
            // limit to any value >= 1 — RadzenNumeric's Min=1 enforces this.
            //
            // SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): the DTO field changed from GroupName
            // (string) to GroupId (Guid). The handler's auto-default loop
            // (Phase 1 in CreateProductCommandHandler) sets a default of 1
            // for every active group; the DTOs we send here are OVERRIDES
            // (Phase 2). Submitting a row with Limit=1 is a no-op (same
            // as the default); submitting Limit=5 overrides the default.
            // Groups not listed (none — every group is listed) keep their
            // default of 1.
            var missingLimitRows = _model.PurchaseLimits
                .Where(r => !r.Limit.HasValue || r.Limit.Value < 1)
                .ToList();

            if (missingLimitRows.Count > 0)
            {
                // Build a friendly error message listing the groups whose
                // limit is missing or invalid.
                var missingNames = missingLimitRows.Select(r => r.GroupName).ToList();
                _submitError = string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["Error_LimitsRequired"], string.Join("، ", missingNames));
                return;
            }

            // All rows have a valid limit — build the DTOs.
            var limitDtos = _model.PurchaseLimits
                .Select(r => new PurchaseLimitInputDto
                {
                    GroupId = r.GroupId,
                    Limit = r.Limit!.Value
                })
                .ToList();

            var command = new CreateProductCommand(
                Name: _model.Name.Trim(),
                Description: _model.Description.Trim(),
                PictureUrl: pictureUrl,
                Price: new MoneyDto
                {
                    Amount = _model.PriceAmount,
                    Currency = _model.PriceCurrency.Trim().ToUpperInvariant()
                },
                InitialStockQuantity: _model.InitialStockQuantity,
                CategoryId: _model.CategoryId.Value,
                SubCategoryId: _model.SubCategoryId,
                SubSubCategoryId: _model.SubSubCategoryId,
                PurchaseLimits: limitDtos);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["CreateSuccess"], _model.Name),
                    summary: Loc["CreateSuccessTitle"]);

                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false);
            }
            else
            {
                _submitError = ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericCreate"];
            }
        }
        catch (FluentValidation.ValidationException vex)
        {
            _submitError = vex.GetJoinedMessages();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // v4 #15: Console.Error.WriteLine dumped ex.GetType().FullName +
            // ex.StackTrace to stdout — replaced with structured ILogger
            // (full exception captured server-side, nothing leaked to
            // container stdout).
            Logger.LogError(ex, "HandleSubmitAsync failed");
            _submitError = ErrorDisplay.Unexpected(UnexpectedErrorCodes.CreateProduct_SubmitFailure);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }
}